<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Roles on tik</title><link>https://tik.projects.metio.wtf/tags/roles/</link><description>Recent content in Roles on tik</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en</language><atom:link href="https://tik.projects.metio.wtf/tags/roles/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Roles and authority</title><link>https://tik.projects.metio.wtf/authoring/roles-and-authority/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://tik.projects.metio.wtf/authoring/roles-and-authority/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;A role is a name a definition uses in its guards. Membership is store&#10;state that decides who is in that role today.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="declaring-a-role"&gt;Declaring a role&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-clojure" data-lang="clojure"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;:process/roles&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;:triager&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;:members&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;&amp;#34;seb&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]}&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="ss"&gt;:approver&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;:members&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;&amp;#34;alice&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;&amp;#34;bob&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]}}&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Guards refer to the name:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-clojure" data-lang="clojure"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;:guards&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;:signed-by&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="ss"&gt;:triager&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;:category&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]]]&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;That guard holds when the fact at &lt;code&gt;[:category]&lt;/code&gt; was asserted by a member of&#10;&lt;code&gt;:triager&lt;/code&gt;. It is a statement about evidence — who put this claim on the&#10;record — rather than a permission check performed somewhere else.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Store administration</title><link>https://tik.projects.metio.wtf/cli/administration/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://tik.projects.metio.wtf/cli/administration/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="identity"&gt;Identity&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;tik actor add alice ~/.config/tik/id_ed25519.pub&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;tik sign &lt;span class="m"&gt;3184&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;tik witness &lt;span class="m"&gt;3184&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;actor add&lt;/code&gt; registers a signer in the store&amp;rsquo;s allowed-signers registry. An&#10;actor name is letters, digits and &lt;code&gt;._@+-&lt;/code&gt;, and the key file holds one&#10;OpenSSH public key on one line; anything else is refused, because the name&#10;and key are written verbatim into the registry, where &lt;code&gt;*&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;?&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;!&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;,&lt;/code&gt;&#10;are principal patterns and a line break starts another grant. A rung-2&#10;binding (&lt;code&gt;tik bridge oidc&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;tik bridge workload&lt;/code&gt;) whose actor or key fails&#10;the same check grants nothing.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>